":"In example 2, we ask how the number of calories in a hot dog is related to the type of hot dog (beef, meat, or poultry). Which is the explanatory variable?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"Type of hot dog","feedback":"Correct! The type of hot dog is claimed to explain differences in calories, so it is the explanatory variable."},{"correct":false,"text":"Number of calories","feedback":"The number of calories is the outcome we are trying to explain—the response variable."}],"multi":false,"hint":"Which variable do we think explains or affects the other?","explanation":""},"key":"TPOcWfoCCH"},{"type":"anywidget","esm":"/textbook/build/quiz-widget-0e29ae0bec3a8408692689b04ac6d4d1.mjs","model":{"question":"In example 6, we ask about the relationship between a driver's age and the maximum distance at which the driver can read a road sign. Which is the response variable?","choices":[{"correct":false,"text":"Driver's age","feedback":"Age is the explanatory variable—it is claimed to affect sign legibility distance."},{"correct":true,"text":"Sign legibility distance","feedback":"Correct! The legibility distance is the outcome we are trying to explain using the driver's age."}],"multi":false,"hint":"Which variable is the outcome being predicted or affected?","explanation":""},"key":"T5y7GVFQCa"},{"type":"anywidget","esm":"/textbook/build/quiz-widget-0e29ae0bec3a8408692689b04ac6d4d1.mjs","model":{"question":"In example 8, we ask whether a person's favorite type of music can be predicted from his or her IQ level. Which is the explanatory variable?","choices":[{"correct":true,"text":"IQ level","feedback":"Correct! IQ level is used as the predictor, so it plays the explanatory role."},{"correct":false,"text":"Favorite type of music","feedback":"Favorite type of music is the outcome being predicted—the response variable."}],"multi":false,"hint":"The predictor is the explanatory variable; the thing being predicted is the response.","explanation":""},"key":"VMLqAgeMgz"}],"key":"